{"at":"-","bindings":"<path>","event":"opened","ir":"c1c49e21565d472d466dc6bfbac29ace179db82e77b990e945649e686c27f03d","prev":null,"protocol":{"description":"Turn an idea into a requirements list (docs/phases.md steps 1 to 3). The idea record is checked against its schema; the idea is dissected into typed items (fact, wish, belief, unknown, ambiguity, dark spot), each citing its span of the idea; every open item becomes an interview question with a default answer, accepted as is or changed, every scope-changing one through the action scope.answer, which needs the capability scope.answer (the runtime grants it per autonomy level: a person at A0 to A2, a decider at A3 and up); the answers are normalised into a requirements list. Every result is a program's exit status, never an LLM's word. A revised dissection invalidates the interview check, a revised interview the requirements check. A revised idea opens a new intake case (the root's intake.open is bound to the idea revision), so this case declares no invalidation from the idea. The case ends passed, or refused when the idea record fails its schema check (nothing here revises the idea); abandoning the idea is the root case's decision. Late findings (docs/trial-2.md, \"The late-finding loop\"): the requirements check also reads the open findings and is not valid while one is open; amend.upstream resolves them by amending the questions and the requirements list.","id":"sdc.intake","revision":9},"seq":0}
